/datum/codex_entry/scannable/fauna/skathari
	name           = "Skathari"

	lore_text      = "The skathari are an unusual, hostile, insectoid species encountered on the fringes of settled space, \
	typically in areas in close proximity to realspace distortions and disturbances such as wormholes or large-scale Casimir \
	condenser use. They are hostile, aggressive, predatory creatures with a strong prey drive and no apparent qualms or \
	difficulties with ingesting and processing any common form of matter into a form of resin.<br><br> \
	Notably, skathari exhibit a natural form of wormhole generation or displacement ability that permits short-ranged \
	teleportation regardless of interference or obstacles in their path. They use this to ambush their prey, which they bombard \
	with venomous spit before descending to employ their claws.<br><br> \
	Although they do not communicate and don't show any form of higher technology, when under direction of a 'tyrant', they \
	exhibit a high degree of coordination and cooperation. It seems likely that they are eusocial organisms with a rigid \
	biological caste system.<br><br> \
	It is highly inadvisable to interact with skathari under any circumstances."

	mechanics_text = "Skathari are violently hostile and have strong ranged and melee attacks. They can even perform a \
	short-range teleport to bypass obstacles and get close to you."

	secret_text    = "Behavioral analysis of skathari nests indicates notable lethargy and high rates of mortality. It seems \
	like that the specimens we encounter in our continuum have been forced out of their home environment and into our own, \
	suggesting a massive central population somewhere within the higher dimensions beyond our instruments and science. A \
	large-scale incursion from this population would likely be disastrous for civilization as a whole."
